      "content": "I get the cost aspect, but it feels like there's a pattern here. You're basically saying we should invest in the white, wealthy neighborhoods to \"maintain\" them, while the Black and Hispanic neighborhoods are seen as too \"volatile\" or \"costly\" to bother with. Isn't that just reinforcing the idea that certain communities aren't worth the investment because of their demographics? Are you saying that the demographic makeup of 90211 makes it a \"bad\" investment compared to the others?",
